#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "Example product: annual census"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "Once a year, every institution reports a set of counts and facts as at a single reference date. That includes enrolment by grade and sex, staff and their qualifications, and facilities and services. The census is the backbone of an education system's official statistics. As a product, it exercises the registries, periodic collection, data quality, indicators, disclosure control and open publication."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "Flow"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "Why it is drawn this way"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "**The registry decides who must respond.** Completeness is measured against the institutions that exist, not against the returns that happened to arrive ([CAP-COLLECTION.1]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "**The head of the institution attests the return.** That puts accountability for the figures with the person who knows them."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "**Review can send a return back.** A query reopens the return with the reviewer's reason, and every change of state is recorded as an event ([CAP-COLLECTION.3]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "**Nothing is computed until the area is complete,** and even then only from a locked snapshot ([CAP-COLLECTION.4]{1}, [CAP-COLLECTION.5]{2})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "The instrument"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "An **instrument** is a versioned file that declares these things:"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "the reference date and the collection window"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "the expected respondents, as a query over the institution registry"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "each item, with its code list, its unit and whether it's required"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "the validation rules, each with its quality dimension and severity ([CAP-QUALITY.4]{1})"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "cross-item checks, such as comparing staff counts with the postings in the registry, or enrolment with last year's enrolment in the grade below"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "A blocking rule stops the return from being submitted, while a warning only needs a reason. Once an instrument is committed it never changes, so next year's census uses a new version."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "The return"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "A return arrives **prefilled** from the registries and last year's accepted return, so respondents confirm and correct figures rather than typing them again. It also **works offline**: someone can complete the form without a connection and synchronise it later, and if they submit twice, the two submissions end up as one return."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "A return moves through these states: not started, in progress, submitted, attested, queried, accepted and locked."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "If a return is missing and the methodology allows **imputation**, every imputed cell is flagged, and the flag is reported with the figure."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "Outputs"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "The census produces:"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "gold counts as at the reference date, from which the semantic layer derives the participation, teacher and facilities indicators ([indicators]{1})"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "completeness and timeliness for each institution and area, reported as measures"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "open tables with permanent identifiers, after disclosure control ([CAP-PUBLICATION]{1})"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "When a late correction arrives, the revision is a new snapshot version. It records the reason, and both versions stay readable."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "Running it as a conformance workload"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "Run these steps on your implementation, and check that each gives the result described."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "Open a census for a fixture registry. The expected respondents should be exactly the registry's active institutions as at the reference date."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "Submit a return with a blocking error. The submission should be refused with a machine-readable error ([CAP-COLLECTION.2]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "Submit the same return twice from an offline client. You should end up with one return."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "Leave one institution's return missing. Its area should read BLOCKED, while the other areas release ([CAP-COLLECTION.4]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "Publish an area that has a small cell. The cell and its complement should be suppressed, and you shouldn't be able to recompute the suppressed value from the totals ([CAP-PUBLICATION.2]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/products/census.md
msgid "Correct an accepted return. A new snapshot version should be created, the published table should gain a new version, and the old version should still be retrievable ([CAP-PUBLICATION.3]{1})."
msgstr ""
